    {
      "key": "GET /api/option-activity/unusual",
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/api/option-activity/unusual",
      "transport": "http-rest",
      "operation": {
        "callbacks": {},
        "description": "Returns option contracts flagged as unusual — the API equivalent of the [live options flow](https://unusualwhales.com/live-options-flow) \"unusual\" view.\n\nThis is the [Hottest Chains](https://api.unusualwhales.com/docs/operations/PublicApi.ScreenerController.contract_screener) screener with the `unusual` preset applied by default: the contract-expressible subset of the live-options-flow criteria — volume > OI, out-of-the-money, DTE ≤ 60, ask-side ≥ 50%, premium ≥ $10k, issue types ADR/Common Stock/ETF.\n\nEvery Hottest Chains filter is accepted here and overrides the preset (e.g. `?min_premium=25000&max_dte=30`); pass `unusual=false` to return the full screen. For the complete list of filters and the response shape see the [Hottest Chains endpoint](https://api.unusualwhales.com/docs/operations/PublicApi.ScreenerController.contract_screener).\n\nFor real time streaming of the same data, subscribe to the `contract_screener` websocket channel, see [https://api.unusualwhales.com/docs/operations/PublicApi.SocketController.contract_screener](https://api.unusualwhales.com/docs/operations/PublicApi.SocketController.contract_screener).\n\nNOTE: Contracts with a volume of less than 200 are not being returned\n",
        "operationId": "PublicApi.ScreenerController.unusual_activity",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "ticker_symbol",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "A comma separated list of tickers. To exclude certain tickers prefix the first ticker with a `-`.",
              "example": "AAPL,INTC",
              "title": "Ticker",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "description": "",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "sectors[]",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "description": "An array of 1 or more sectors.",
